Content:
@Agenxy _may_ also have some pertinent suggestions (once things are further along; there's some primitive devices I really want models for and the SCL stuff can wait until there's time left and the primitives are succesfully PnR'd) on affordably-enough-in-area-overhead and with enough ability to calibrate out muxing harnesses:
ways to also measure DUT capacitances as needed for modeling AC behavior, not just DC operating points as the plain "muxed e-test" (with kelvin connections to calibrate out the MUX resistance) does.

(Personally I'm not so sure that needs measuring by us like this, but idk for sure. I'd _expect_ the existing RLC e-test structures on iirc Run2 can sufficciently de-embed muxing-tolerant RLC measurement tactics that can affordable provide detailed statistical distribution data, with which then model/extraction fit tuning could be done using the measured DC op point behavior to find SPICE model fits of parasitics that together with the known statistics of DC behavior of DUTs can accurately explain compound-DUT-arrangements behavior under AC conditions.)
